# TESTIMONIUM — Planned Additions & Improvements: Implementation Plan

This plan covers the 8 planned features from `TESTIMONIUM_PLANNED_ADDITIONS_AND_IMPROVEMENTS.md`, grounded in the current schema, services, and architecture. Phases are ordered to minimize blocking dependencies.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The following decisions must be resolved before or during their respective phases. They affect schema design, business logic, and UI copy.

| # | Question | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 | Are `WEDDING`, `MARRIAGE_SPECIAL`, and `FUNERAL` **absolutely** forbidden on Sundays (non-overridable), or may a parish create a specific-date Sunday override? | Phase A DB schema, `BookingValidator.js` |
| Q2 | Are weekday availability rules **parish-wide**, **service-specific**, or **both**? | Phase A DB schema |
| Q3 | Which roles can edit scheduling availability? (Secretary only, or Priest too?) | Phase A API auth middleware |
| Q4 | What visibility should **existing** `parish_events` receive after the migration? (`PUBLIC` is safest default) | Phase B migration script |
| Q5 | Can Priests change event visibility? | Phase B API middleware |
| Q6 | Can Priests create `DailyReport` records? | Phase C schema/API |
| Q7 | Should reports be **deletable** (hard delete) or **archivable** (soft delete)? | Phase C schema |
| Q8 | Should reports support photo/file attachments? | Phase C schema |
| Q9 | Can a Diocese Coordinator create a report without selecting a specific parish? | Phase C API validation |
| Q10 | Which email provider will be used? (Resend, SendGrid, Nodemailer+SMTP, etc.) | Phase F `EmailService.js` |
| Q11 | Should parishioners be able to opt out of non-essential emails? | Phase F schema/Notification model |
| Q12 | Should Help content be static (in-source) initially, or CMS-driven from day one? | Phase G |

