## Phase F — Email Notifications

**Goal:** Send transactional emails on key workflow transitions. Email failures must never corrupt workflow state.

### Phase F — Backend

#### Decision required: Q10 (email provider)

Recommended architecture regardless of provider: a thin `EmailService.js` wrapper isolates provider SDK calls so the provider can be swapped without touching business logic.

#### [MODIFY] [`schema.prisma`](file:///c:/Users/me/Documents/testimonium/testimonium-backend/prisma/schema.prisma)

New model for delivery logging:

```prisma
enum EmailNotificationStatus {
  QUEUED
  SENT
  FAILED
  SKIPPED
}

model EmailNotificationLog {
  id               Int                     @id @default(autoincrement()) @map("email_log_id")
  recipientEmail   String                  @map("recipient_email") @db.VarChar(150)
  emailType        String                  @map("email_type") @db.VarChar(100)  // e.g. "DOCUMENT_READY_FOR_PICKUP"
  referenceType    String?                 @map("reference_type") @db.VarChar(50)
  referenceId      Int?                    @map("reference_id")
  status           EmailNotificationStatus @default(QUEUED)
  failureReason    String?                 @map("failure_reason") @db.Text
  retryCount       Int                     @default(0) @map("retry_count")
  queuedAt         DateTime                @default(now()) @map("queued_at")
  sentAt           DateTime?               @map("sent_at")

  @@index([referenceType, referenceId])
  @@index([status])
  @@map("email_notification_logs")
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> If the existing `notifications` table is extended to track email delivery directly, a separate log model may not be necessary. Evaluate against Q10 provider capabilities.

#### [NEW] [`EmailService.js`](file:///c:/Users/me/Documents/testimonium/testimonium-backend/services/EmailService.js)

Provider-agnostic wrapper:
- `sendEmail({ to, subject, html, textFallback })` — calls provider SDK.
- Returns `{ success: boolean, messageId?: string, error?: string }`.
- Logs to `EmailNotificationLog`.
- **Never throws**; errors are caught and logged.

#### [NEW] `email-templates/` directory

HTML + text templates for each notification type. Template engine: either simple string interpolation or `@mjml/core` for responsive email layouts.

| Template | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `document-ready-for-pickup.html` | `DocumentRequestStatus → READY_FOR_PICKUP` |
| `schedule-submitted.html` | Parishioner submits schedule request |
| `schedule-proposed-reschedule.html` | Secretary proposes new date/time |
| `schedule-confirmed.html` | Schedule status → `CONFIRMED` |

#### [MODIFY] [`NotificationDispatcher.js`](file:///c:/Users/me/Documents/testimonium/testimonium-backend/services/NotificationDispatcher.js)

After each in-app notification is created and the DB commit succeeds, call `EmailService.js` for applicable transitions. Wrap email call in `try/catch`; log failure without re-throwing.

**Deduplication:** Before sending, query `EmailNotificationLog` for an existing row with the same `emailType + referenceType + referenceId`. If found and status is `SENT`, skip and log `SKIPPED`.

#### [MODIFY] [`DocumentRequestService.js`](file:///c:/Users/me/Documents/testimonium/testimonium-backend/services/DocumentRequestService.js) and [`ScheduleService.js`](file:///c:/Users/me/Documents/testimonium/testimonium-backend/services/ScheduleService.js)

Ensure that the `NotificationDispatcher` (and therefore email) is always invoked **after** the database transaction commits successfully.

